  "id": "COMPOUND:17374 - PROTEIN:5168",
  "verbalization": "Mollicellin N is implicated in the inhibition of MLMA through multiple distinct pathways, each involving a different target. The first pathway links Mollicellin N to NCI-H524, which is a target of 3Beta-Hydroxyolean-12-En-23,29-Dioic Acid, and ultimately to MLMA. The second pathway connects Mollicellin N to A704, which is also targeted by the same compound, leading to the same final target. The third pathway involves Mollicellin N targeting P2X purinoceptor 1, which is inhibited by [(1R)-1-[(5Z)-4-Bromo-5-(Bromomethylidene)-2-Oxofuran-3-Yl]Butyl] Acetate, and again leading to MLMA. These pathways suggest that Mollicellin N exerts its effects through different molecular mechanisms, yet all converge on MLMA as a downstream target. The evidence supports a direct relationship between Mollicellin N and MLMA, with the core mechanism likely involving the inhibition of a key enzyme or receptor that ultimately affects MLMA. The integration of these pathways highlights the complexity of the interaction, but the consistent targeting of MLMA across different targets reinforces the potential for a mechanistic link.",
